s/having-a-stubble-seems-like-a-really-good-looksmax.185776/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220724231123/https://looksmax.org/threads/having-a-stubble-seems-like-a-really-good-looksmax.185776/"},{"title":"brando with goatee","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/brando-with-goatee.105478/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240228035553/https://looksmax.org/threads/brando-with-goatee.105478/"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Chinstrap / goatee / designer stubble styling — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Goatee"},{"title":"Goatee - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goatee"},{"title":"Beard - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beard"},{"title":"Stubble - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stubble"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Jawline & face shape","chain":["Choose a limited beard style","Work around patchy growth","Altered face shape and chin look"],"effect":"direct","text":"Keeping hair only in selected zones works around patchy growth and adds contrast, chin projection and framing to the lower face. How it looks depends on your growth pattern and jaw."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Goatee","lead":["Chinstrap, goatee and designer-stubble styling refers to shaping facial hair into limited patterns to work around patchy growth or to alter perceived face shape. Wikipedia defines a goatee as chin hair without cheek hair, a term that broadened by the 1990s to cover chin styles generally.[1]","Users on looksmax.org discuss stubble and goatees as ways to add contrast to the lower face, and also report that results depend on growth pattern and jaw structure.[2][3] No clinical studies were found on these styles."],"infobox":[["Type","Facial hair styling"],["Styles","Goatee, chinstrap, Van Dyke, designer stubble"],["Evidence status","Untested (appearance claims anecdotal)"]],"sections":[{"h":"Styles","paras":["A goatee places hair on the chin entirely; debate exists over whether chin-only styles should be called goatees or Van Dykes.[1] Designer stubble is described as a stubble type that became popular in the 1980s, and stubble near a \"two-day shadow\" was fashionable in 2010.[4][5]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"History","paras":["Goatee-like styles trace to depictions of Pan in classical antiquity; the style returned with 1950s beatniks and was fashionable again in the 1990s.[1] Grokipedia also links the Van Dyke to the painter Anthony van Dyck in 17th-century Europe, though that source is AI-generated.[6]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Use in looksmaxxing","paras":["One poster used a goatee as a short-term measure before chin filler, saying it added contrast.[2] Another reported that stubble made their jawline look less defined from the side and recommended checking multiple angles and growth pattern.[3]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found. Studies of beard perception broadly are outside this entry."],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"Forum users discuss stubble and goatees as tools for contrast and for hiding patchy growth, with mixed personal reports.[2][3]","claims":[{"claim":"A goatee adds chin projection and contrast.","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Stubble can make the jaw look less defined, depending on growth pattern.","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[{"year":"1950s","event":"Goatee returns with beatniks.[1]"},{"year":"1980s","event":"Designer stubble becomes popular.[4]"},{"year":"1990s","event":"Goatees fashionable across professions.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Goatee - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goatee","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Goatee for chin to philtrum, forward projection","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/goatee-for-chin-to-philtrum-forward-projection.1298313/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2024,"type":"forum"},{"title":"Stubble really looks like shit on me","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/